# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste in your Mapbox PUBLIC token.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Get one at https://console.mapbox.com/account/access-tokens/
#
# It MUST be a public token (starts with `pk.`). Public tokens are designed to be
# shipped to the browser — mapbox-gl cannot work without one client-side.
#
# NEVER put a secret token (`sk.`) here. Secret tokens carry write scopes and this
# value is bundled into the client build, where anyone can read it.
#
# Before deploying, add a URL restriction to the token in the Mapbox console so it
# only works from your domain. Note that a restricted token rejects requests with
# HTTP 403, which is a confusing symptom — check restrictions first when debugging.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=pk.your_token_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics (optional)
#
# The GA4 measurement ID, `G-XXXXXXXXXX`. Unlike the Mapbox token this is not a
# secret — it travels in every request the tag makes, and it has to, because it
# is how Google knows which property the data belongs to.
#
# Leave it blank and analytics never starts AND the consent banner never
# appears: there is no point asking permission to do nothing. See
# `src/analytics/index.ts`.
#
# Filling it in locally gets you the banner but never the tag — `gtag.js` is
# only loaded in a production build, so you can work on the consent flow
# without putting test events into a real property.
#
# Find it in the GA4 console under Admin → Data streams → your web stream.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

